WEBVTT

1
00:01:35.715 --> 00:01:40.006
JOEL:
"Random thoughts
for Valentine's Day, 2004.

2
00:01:41.756 --> 00:01:44.964
"Today is a holiday invented
by greeting-card companies

3
00:01:45.798 --> 00:01:48.173
"to make people
feel like crap.

4
00:01:51.882 --> 00:01:53.797
"I ditched work today.

5
00:01:56.132 --> 00:01:58.380
"Took a train out to Montauk.

6
00:02:00.548 --> 00:02:02.255
"I don't know why.

7
00:02:04.007 --> 00:02:06.213
"I'm not an impulsive person.

8
00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:16.922
"I guess I just woke up
in a funk this morning.

9
00:02:17.423 --> 00:02:19.213
"I gotta get my car fixed."

10
00:02:19.882 --> 00:02:22.089
Hi, Cindy. It's Joel.

11
00:02:24.631 --> 00:02:27.172
Listen, I don't feel
very well today.

12
00:02:28.256 --> 00:02:30.089
No, food poisoning,
I think.

13
00:02:30.882 --> 00:02:33.464
JOEL:
"It's goddamn freezing
on this beach.

14
00:02:33.882 --> 00:02:36.464
"Montauk in February.
Brilliant, Joel.

15
00:02:39.214 --> 00:02:42.213
"Pages ripped out.
Don't remember doing that.

16
00:02:45.381 --> 00:02:48.422
"It appears this is
my first entry in two years.

17
00:02:57.631 --> 00:02:59.380
"Sand is overrated.

18
00:03:00.548 --> 00:03:02.714
"It's just tiny little rocks.

19
00:03:12.381 --> 00:03:14.839
"If only I could
meet someone new.

20
00:03:15.965 --> 00:03:17.755
"I guess my chances
of that happening

21
00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:19.380
"are somewhat diminished,

22
00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:23.213
"since I'm incapable
of making eye contact
with a woman I don't know.

23
00:03:24.590 --> 00:03:28.881
"Maybe I should
get back together with Naomi.
She was nice.

24
00:03:29.965 --> 00:03:31.464
"Nice is good.

25
00:03:33.423 --> 00:03:34.922
"She loved me.

26
00:04:12.173 --> 00:04:15.297
"Why do I fall in love
with every woman I see

27
00:04:15.381 --> 00:04:18.088
"who shows me
the least bit of attention?"

28
00:04:59.715 --> 00:05:00.714
Hi.

29
00:05:01.465 --> 00:05:03.547
I'm sorry?
I just said hi.

30
00:05:04.339 --> 00:05:05.714
Hi, hello.

31
00:05:07.089 --> 00:05:08.881
Okay if I sit closer?

32
00:05:11.631 --> 00:05:13.213
How far are you going?

33
00:05:13.756 --> 00:05:15.338
Rockville Center.

34
00:05:15.423 --> 00:05:17.046
Get out. Me, too.

35
00:05:17.548 --> 00:05:18.505
Really?

36
00:05:18.590 --> 00:05:19.589
What are the odds?

37
00:05:22.423 --> 00:05:24.255
Listen, do I know you?

38
00:05:27.715 --> 00:05:29.422
Do you ever shop
at Barnes and Noble?

39
00:05:29.506 --> 00:05:30.672
Sure.

40
00:05:30.756 --> 00:05:32.380
That's it!
Yeah?

41
00:05:32.465 --> 00:05:33.963
I've seen you, man.

42
00:05:34.590 --> 00:05:38.297
Book slave there
for five years now.

43
00:05:38.882 --> 00:05:39.922
Jesus!

44
00:05:40.006 --> 00:05:42.005
I would have thought
I would remember you.

45
00:05:42.089 --> 00:05:43.922
It might be the hair.

46
00:05:44.006 --> 00:05:45.005
What might?

47
00:05:45.089 --> 00:05:46.922
It changes a lot,
the color.

48
00:05:47.173 --> 00:05:49.422
That's why you might
not recognize me.

49
00:05:49.590 --> 00:05:51.547
It's called Blue Ruin.
Right.

50
00:05:51.631 --> 00:05:53.630
The color.
Snappy name, huh?

51
00:05:53.715 --> 00:05:54.922
I like it.

52
00:05:58.214 --> 00:06:01.797
This company makes
a whole line of colors
with equally snappy names.

53
00:06:01.882 --> 00:06:05.464
You've got Red Menace,
Yellow Fever,
Green Revolution.

54
00:06:06.590 --> 00:06:08.839
That would be a job,
coming up with those names.

55
00:06:08.923 --> 00:06:11.797
You think there could
possibly be a job like that?

56
00:06:11.882 --> 00:06:15.630
I mean, how many hair colors
could there be? 15 maybe?

57
00:06:16.047 --> 00:06:18.005
Someone's got that job.

58
00:06:19.006 --> 00:06:21.630
Agent Orange.
I came up with that one.

59
00:06:22.798 --> 00:06:25.213
I apply my personality
in a paste.

60
00:06:25.715 --> 00:06:27.547
I doubt that very much.

61
00:06:28.631 --> 00:06:32.714
Well, you don't know me,
so you don't know, do you?

62
00:06:36.214 --> 00:06:39.839
I'm sorry.
I was just trying to be nice.

63
00:06:41.548 --> 00:06:43.380
Yeah. I got it.

64
00:07:03.047 --> 00:07:04.839
My name's Clementine,
by the way.

65
00:07:04.922 --> 00:07:06.088
I'm Joel.

66
00:07:06.590 --> 00:07:07.880
Hi, Joel.

67
00:07:09.214 --> 00:07:10.921
No jokes about my name.

68
00:07:11.006 --> 00:07:13.172
Oh, no.
You wouldn't do that.

69
00:07:13.256 --> 00:07:14.963
You're trying to be nice.

70
00:07:15.590 --> 00:07:18.005
I don't know any jokes
about your name.

71
00:07:18.089 --> 00:07:19.755
Huckleberry Hound.

72
00:07:21.339 --> 00:07:23.213
I don't know
what that means.

73
00:07:23.298 --> 00:07:25.963
Huckleberry Hound?
What are you, nuts?

74
00:07:26.131 --> 00:07:27.880
It's been suggested.

75
00:07:28.131 --> 00:07:31.589
Oh, my darling, oh, my darling
Oh, my darling Clementine

76
00:07:31.881 --> 00:07:36.422
You are lost and gone forever
Dreadful sorry, Clementine

77
00:07:36.964 --> 00:07:37.963
No?

78
00:07:38.047 --> 00:07:39.422
I'm sorry.

79
00:07:40.214 --> 00:07:42.338
It's a pretty name, though.
It really is nice.

80
00:07:42.423 --> 00:07:46.380
It means merciful, right?
Clemency?

81
00:07:47.214 --> 00:07:48.838
Although it hardly fits.

82
00:07:48.922 --> 00:07:51.213
I'm a vindictive little bitch,
truth be told.

83
00:07:51.298 --> 00:07:53.338
I wouldn't think that
about you.

84
00:07:53.423 --> 00:07:55.630
Why wouldn't you think that
about me?

85
00:07:56.214 --> 00:07:57.714
I don't know.

86
00:08:01.715 --> 00:08:03.297
You seem nice.

87
00:08:03.756 --> 00:08:05.380
Now I'm nice?

88
00:08:05.964 --> 00:08:08.630
Oh, God, don't you know
any other adjectives?

89
00:08:08.715 --> 00:08:11.464
I don't need nice.
I don't need myself to be it

90
00:08:11.548 --> 00:08:13.422
and I don't need anybody
to be it at me.

91
00:08:13.506 --> 00:08:14.630
Okay.

92
00:08:20.797 --> 00:08:22.130
It's Joel, right?

93
00:08:23.423 --> 00:08:24.505
Yes.

94
00:08:26.047 --> 00:08:27.838
I'm sorry I yelled at you.

95
00:08:28.590 --> 00:08:30.963
I'm a little
out of sorts today.

96
00:08:40.797 --> 00:08:42.464
My embarrassing admission

97
00:08:42.548 --> 00:08:45.088
is I really like
that you're nice right now.

98
00:08:46.881 --> 00:08:50.630
I can't tell
from one moment to the next
what I'm going to like,

99
00:08:50.715 --> 00:08:54.213
but right now
I'm glad you are.

100
00:09:02.881 --> 00:09:05.880
I have some stuff
that I probably should...

101
00:09:08.548 --> 00:09:11.130
I'm writing...
I'm sorry. Okay.

102
00:09:11.214 --> 00:09:12.880
No.
Sure. That's okay.

103
00:09:16.006 --> 00:09:17.838
Take care, then.

104
00:09:17.922 --> 00:09:19.046
Jesus.

105
00:09:34.673 --> 00:09:37.464
I could give you a ride
if you need.

106
00:09:38.465 --> 00:09:39.547
It's cold.

107
00:09:40.214 --> 00:09:42.464
Yeah! Okay. It is frosty.

108
00:09:43.173 --> 00:09:45.130
You're not a stalker
or anything, right?

109
00:09:45.214 --> 00:09:48.005
I'm not a stalker.
You're the one
that talked to me, remember?

110
00:09:48.089 --> 00:09:50.297
That is the oldest trick
in the stalker book.

111
00:09:50.381 --> 00:09:52.838
Really?
There's a stalker book?

112
00:09:55.714 --> 00:09:57.464
I've got to read that one.

113
00:10:02.548 --> 00:10:05.338
Look, I'm sorry
if I came off sort of nutso.

114
00:10:05.922 --> 00:10:07.213
I'm not really.

115
00:10:07.298 --> 00:10:10.464
That's okay.
I didn't think you were.

116
00:10:16.839 --> 00:10:19.005
Do you want
to have a drink?

117
00:10:19.256 --> 00:10:21.672
I have lots of drinks,
and I could...

118
00:10:24.339 --> 00:10:27.796
Never mind.
Sorry, that was stupid.
I'm embarrassed now.

119
00:10:27.881 --> 00:10:29.505
Good night, Joel.

120
00:10:49.381 --> 00:10:51.005
Two Blue Ruins.

121
00:10:53.298 --> 00:10:54.297
Thank you.

122
00:10:54.381 --> 00:10:55.671
Drink up, young man.

123
00:10:56.714 --> 00:10:59.671
It'll make
the whole seduction part
less repugnant.

124
00:11:03.381 --> 00:11:05.754
I'm just kidding!
Come on.

125
00:11:12.506 --> 00:11:14.796
You're kind of close-mouthed,
aren't you?

126
00:11:14.881 --> 00:11:16.046
I'm sorry.

127
00:11:17.797 --> 00:11:20.589
You know, my life isn't
that interesting.

128
00:11:22.047 --> 00:11:24.464
I go to work, I come home.

129
00:11:25.714 --> 00:11:27.713
I don't know what to say.

130
00:11:28.590 --> 00:11:30.547
You should read my journal.

131
00:11:31.256 --> 00:11:34.380
I mean, it's just blank.

132
00:11:34.922 --> 00:11:38.088
Really? Does that
make you sad or anxious?

133
00:11:38.173 --> 00:11:41.629
I'm always anxious,
thinking I'm not living
my life to the fullest.

134
00:11:41.714 --> 00:11:43.629
Taking advantage
of every possibility

135
00:11:43.714 --> 00:11:47.422
and making sure
I'm not wasting one second
of the little time I have.

136
00:11:47.506 --> 00:11:49.754
I think about that.
Yeah?

137
00:11:54.506 --> 00:11:56.297
You're really nice.

138
00:11:57.089 --> 00:11:59.505
God, I have to stop
saying that.

139
00:12:01.672 --> 00:12:04.255
I'm gonna marry you.
I know it.

140
00:12:07.047 --> 00:12:08.172
Okay.

141
00:12:13.173 --> 00:12:17.213
Joel, you should
come up to the Charles
with me sometime.

142
00:12:17.714 --> 00:12:19.547
It gets frozen
this time of year.

143
00:12:19.630 --> 00:12:21.629
That sounds scary.
Exactly.

144
00:12:22.630 --> 00:12:25.547
I'll pack a picnic,
a night picnic.

145
00:12:26.131 --> 00:12:28.046
Night picnics are different.

146
00:12:29.797 --> 00:12:31.464
That sounds good.

147
00:12:32.547 --> 00:12:34.629
But I should go now.

148
00:12:36.047 --> 00:12:37.297
You should stay.

149
00:12:37.381 --> 00:12:38.754
No, I really have...

150
00:12:39.797 --> 00:12:41.422
I have to get up
so early and...

151
00:12:41.506 --> 00:12:43.297
I would like you
to call me.

152
00:12:43.381 --> 00:12:45.796
Would you do that?
I'd like it.

153
00:12:45.881 --> 00:12:46.880
Yes.

154
00:12:51.381 --> 00:12:54.422
Wish me
a happy Valentine's Day
when you call.

155
00:12:54.797 --> 00:12:56.172
That'd be nice.

156
00:13:37.256 --> 00:13:39.088
CLEMENTINE:
What took you so long?

157
00:13:39.173 --> 00:13:40.754
I just walked in.

158
00:13:42.256 --> 00:13:43.671
You miss me?

159
00:13:45.047 --> 00:13:46.546
Oddly enough, I do.

160
00:13:47.839 --> 00:13:50.754
You said "I do."
I guess that means
we're married.

161
00:13:50.964 --> 00:13:52.338
I guess so.

162
00:13:52.964 --> 00:13:55.463
Tomorrow night?
Honeymoon on ice?

163
00:13:55.839 --> 00:13:58.046
It's really solid
this time of year.

164
00:13:59.006 --> 00:14:01.588
I don't know.
Come on.

165
00:14:09.672 --> 00:14:11.255
It's so beautiful.

166
00:14:12.672 --> 00:14:13.921
Isn't it?

167
00:14:18.214 --> 00:14:19.588
Don't go too far.

168
00:14:22.339 --> 00:14:23.713
Are you okay?

169
00:14:28.214 --> 00:14:29.546
Oh, my ass!

170
00:14:31.964 --> 00:14:34.463
I think I should go back.
Come on!

171
00:14:34.547 --> 00:14:36.046
But what if it breaks?

172
00:14:36.131 --> 00:14:38.504
"What if?"
Do you really care
right now?

173
00:14:39.381 --> 00:14:41.005
Come here, please.

174
00:14:48.881 --> 00:14:51.255
Slidey-slidey.

175
00:14:51.714 --> 00:14:53.380
This looks good.

176
00:14:53.922 --> 00:14:55.297
Let me show you
this one thing.

177
00:14:55.381 --> 00:14:57.213
What are you doing?

178
00:14:59.839 --> 00:15:01.046
Come on.

179
00:15:06.505 --> 00:15:08.380
Think I heard a crack.

180
00:15:08.881 --> 00:15:11.963
It's not going to crack.
Or break.

181
00:15:12.047 --> 00:15:13.504
It's so thick.

182
00:15:16.047 --> 00:15:18.796
Show me
which constellations
you know.

183
00:15:21.547 --> 00:15:23.421
I don't know any.

184
00:15:25.298 --> 00:15:27.297
Show me which ones
you know.

185
00:15:27.380 --> 00:15:28.379
Okay.

186
00:15:34.714 --> 00:15:36.088
There's Osidius.

187
00:15:36.380 --> 00:15:37.379
Where?

188
00:15:38.339 --> 00:15:39.963
Right there. See?

189
00:15:40.339 --> 00:15:42.546
A sort of a swoop
and a cross.

190
00:15:43.214 --> 00:15:44.963
Osidius the Emphatic.

191
00:15:47.006 --> 00:15:48.463
You're full of shit, right?

192
00:15:48.547 --> 00:15:50.671
No. Osidius, right there.

193
00:15:51.214 --> 00:15:52.796
Swoop and a cross.

194
00:15:52.881 --> 00:15:54.713
Shut the fuck up!

195
00:16:09.338 --> 00:16:10.963
Cock-a-doodle-doo.

196
00:16:15.755 --> 00:16:18.588
Sorry to wake you,
but we're here.

197
00:16:28.214 --> 00:16:30.546
Can I come over
to your house,

198
00:16:31.714 --> 00:16:34.880
to sleep? I'm so tired.

199
00:16:36.630 --> 00:16:39.213
Okay. Yeah, sure.

200
00:16:39.922 --> 00:16:41.713
Let me get my toothbrush.

201
00:17:04.505 --> 00:17:05.588
Yes?

202
00:17:06.338 --> 00:17:07.880
Can I help you?

203
00:17:08.464 --> 00:17:10.046
What do you mean?

204
00:17:10.881 --> 00:17:13.130
Can I help you
with something?

205
00:17:14.089 --> 00:17:15.213
No.

206
00:17:16.505 --> 00:17:18.005
What are you doing here?

207
00:17:18.089 --> 00:17:20.796
I'm not really sure
what you're asking me.

208
00:17:23.839 --> 00:17:25.046
Thanks.

209
00:19:13.338 --> 00:19:15.088
STAN:
We're looking for 159.

210
00:19:15.172 --> 00:19:16.421
PATRICK:
What number is that?

211
00:19:16.505 --> 00:19:17.880
I don't know
what number that is.

212
00:19:17.964 --> 00:19:20.421
Jesus Christ.
You'd think they'd
light the number

213
00:19:20.505 --> 00:19:21.838
or at least put
a number on...

214
00:19:21.922 --> 00:19:23.254
Is that him?
I think so.

215
00:19:23.338 --> 00:19:24.963
Yeah, that's him.

216
00:19:25.464 --> 00:19:26.754
That's him.

217
00:19:41.672 --> 00:19:43.713
Hey, Joel.
Frank.

218
00:19:47.547 --> 00:19:48.713
Shit.

219
00:19:49.380 --> 00:19:53.171
Jesus. The only
Valentine's Day cards I get
are from my mother.

220
00:19:53.255 --> 00:19:55.212
How pathetic is that?

221
00:19:55.630 --> 00:19:58.838
You're lucky
you have Clementine.
She is way cool.

222
00:19:59.213 --> 00:20:01.838
You got any
big Valentine's Day plans
with her?

223
00:20:05.797 --> 00:20:06.880
No.

224
00:20:07.006 --> 00:20:10.129
It's only a day away.
Better make some
reservations or something.

225
00:20:10.213 --> 00:20:12.421
Don't want to end up
at Mickey D's, right?

226
00:20:12.505 --> 00:20:13.838
McRomance!

227
00:20:14.006 --> 00:20:15.754
You want some fries
with that shake?

228
00:20:15.839 --> 00:20:19.129
I have to go to sleep now,
Frank.

229
00:20:20.047 --> 00:20:21.129
It's 8:30.

230
00:20:49.839 --> 00:20:51.504
STAN: Patrick, stop it.

231
00:21:10.172 --> 00:21:12.045
Okay.

232
00:21:19.046 --> 00:21:20.963
PATRICK:
Showtime at the Apollo.

233
00:21:33.213 --> 00:21:34.379
Quiet.

234
00:21:43.881 --> 00:21:45.504
STAN: Get it off your head.

235
00:21:48.213 --> 00:21:50.004
FRANK: Hey, Joel.
What's up?

236
00:21:51.464 --> 00:21:52.796
Hi, Frank.

237
00:21:58.380 --> 00:22:02.713
I only get Valentine's Day
cards from my mom.
How pathetic is that?

238
00:22:04.213 --> 00:22:06.713
You're lucky
you have Clementine, Joel.

239
00:22:07.005 --> 00:22:10.379
You got any
big Valentine's Day plans
with her?

240
00:22:11.672 --> 00:22:12.713
No.

241
00:22:13.172 --> 00:22:16.713
It's only a day away.
Better make
a reservation somewhere.

242
00:22:17.338 --> 00:22:19.629
Don't want to end up
at Mickey D's.

243
00:22:20.672 --> 00:22:22.337
Oh, no.
JOEL: Yes.

244
00:22:22.422 --> 00:22:25.880
Valentine's Day
is three days away.
I want it resolved.

245
00:22:26.213 --> 00:22:28.129
I'm willing to be the one
to resolve it.

246
00:22:28.213 --> 00:22:31.212
So I call her,
and she's changed
her number.

247
00:22:31.589 --> 00:22:34.796
JOEL: So I walked over
to Antic Attic
to get her something.

248
00:22:34.881 --> 00:22:38.504
I thought I'd go over to work,
give her an early Valentine.

249
00:22:40.464 --> 00:22:42.337
And you won't believe it.

250
00:22:42.589 --> 00:22:46.045
She's there with this guy,

251
00:22:46.714 --> 00:22:48.588
this really young guy.

252
00:22:49.046 --> 00:22:52.546
And she looks at me like
she doesn't even know
who I am.

253
00:22:53.172 --> 00:22:54.212
Excuse me?

254
00:22:55.213 --> 00:22:56.796
Can I help you
find something, sir?

255
00:23:00.797 --> 00:23:02.337
PATRICK: Hey, Clem-ato.

256
00:23:03.172 --> 00:23:06.212
Patrick! Baby boy!

257
00:23:09.589 --> 00:23:11.004
What are you doing here,
baby?

258
00:23:11.088 --> 00:23:12.463
Just came to surprise you.

259
00:23:12.547 --> 00:23:15.045
Let me know
if you need something, sir.

260
