to hold your hand. Come on.

765
00:53:27.378 --> 00:53:28.586
JOEL: Stop it!

766
00:53:31.128 --> 00:53:33.044
I could die right now.

767
00:53:35.378 --> 00:53:39.544
I'm just so happy.

768
00:53:43.045 --> 00:53:45.169
I've never felt
that before.

769
00:53:48.503 --> 00:53:50.210
I'm just exactly

770
00:53:53.295 --> 00:53:54.961
where I want to be.

771
00:54:04.587 --> 00:54:08.003
I want to call it off.
I'll give you a sign.

772
00:54:13.795 --> 00:54:15.669
I want to call it off.

773
00:54:17.462 --> 00:54:21.752
Can you hear me?
I don't want this anymore!
I want to call it off!

774
00:54:28.879 --> 00:54:31.377
Is anybody there?

775
00:54:48.712 --> 00:54:50.794
What?
We've got to go.

776
00:54:50.879 --> 00:54:53.919
Where?
I have an idea
of how to stop this.

777
00:54:54.003 --> 00:54:55.252
Stop what?

778
00:55:01.044 --> 00:55:02.961
JOEL: Don't tickle me. No.

779
00:55:03.044 --> 00:55:04.878
CLEMENTINE: Smell my pits!

780
00:55:05.879 --> 00:55:07.544
Concentrate, Clem.

781
00:55:08.712 --> 00:55:11.043
JOEL: We have to get back
to the office.
CLEMENTINE: Halloween.

782
00:55:11.128 --> 00:55:13.878
There was a tape recorder.
No, not the picture.

783
00:55:16.920 --> 00:55:18.627
Back here. Come on.

784
00:55:19.336 --> 00:55:22.252
CLEMENTINE: Look at me.
I want to go there.

785
00:55:22.378 --> 00:55:26.794
DR. MIERZWIAK:
Our files are confidential,
so I can't show you evidence.

786
00:55:27.378 --> 00:55:31.002
Suffice it to say
that Miss Kruczynski

787
00:55:31.086 --> 00:55:34.544
was not happy
and she wanted to move on.

788
00:55:36.003 --> 00:55:37.335
Tell me about...

789
00:55:37.420 --> 00:55:40.502
JOEL: Tell me
everything you remember.
That's what he said.

790
00:55:40.587 --> 00:55:42.544
CLEMENTINE: What did we
see that day?

791
00:55:42.628 --> 00:55:46.419
We're going to see
my grandma.
Shit!

792
00:55:46.837 --> 00:55:49.002
CLEMENTINE: Joel, why...
JOEL: No. We're not
going on a train.

793
00:55:49.086 --> 00:55:51.252
Joel, please.
Don't make me run anymore.

794
00:55:51.336 --> 00:55:52.627
Come on.

795
00:55:52.712 --> 00:55:53.711
Mierzwiak!

796
00:55:54.961 --> 00:55:57.002
Do we always have to run?

797
00:56:07.712 --> 00:56:08.878
Please?

798
00:56:10.044 --> 00:56:14.669
Why don't we begin by
you telling me everything
you can remember...

799
00:56:14.753 --> 00:56:17.544
JOEL: Mierzwiak,
wake me up!

800
00:56:19.462 --> 00:56:23.627
I'm sorry, Mr. Barish,
I thought you understood
what was going on.

801
00:56:24.587 --> 00:56:28.294
You're erasing her from me.
You're erasing me from her.

802
00:56:34.044 --> 00:56:37.169
You got this thing.
I'm in my bed. I know it.

803
00:56:38.211 --> 00:56:39.544
I'm in my brain.

804
00:56:39.628 --> 00:56:42.960
I'm part of
your imagination, too.

805
00:56:43.044 --> 00:56:45.918
How can I help
you from there?

806
00:56:46.003 --> 00:56:48.878
I'm inside your head, too.
I'm you.

807
00:56:51.879 --> 00:56:53.085
Sorry.

808
00:56:53.211 --> 00:56:54.752
Look, who's that?

809
00:56:55.253 --> 00:56:57.586
He works for us.

810
00:56:57.670 --> 00:57:02.043
That's Patrick,

811
00:57:02.295 --> 00:57:04.169
baby boy.

812
00:57:04.712 --> 00:57:08.377
He's stealing my identity.
He stole my stuff.

813
00:57:09.919 --> 00:57:13.294
He's seducing my girlfriend
with my words and my things.

814
00:57:13.378 --> 00:57:15.294
He stole her underwear.

815
00:57:16.086 --> 00:57:18.711
Jesus Christ.
He stole her underwear.

816
00:57:20.003 --> 00:57:21.669
I could die right now, Clem.

817
00:57:22.211 --> 00:57:23.210
I'm just happy.

818
00:57:24.837 --> 00:57:26.544
I've never felt that before.

819
00:57:27.003 --> 00:57:28.627
I'm exactly
where I want to be.

820
00:57:31.086 --> 00:57:32.752
I want to go home.

821
00:57:34.878 --> 00:57:36.002
What?

822
00:57:41.961 --> 00:57:43.335
Wait, Clem.

823
00:57:45.712 --> 00:57:48.377
Clem, they're erasing you.

824
00:57:49.753 --> 00:57:51.085
CLEMENTINE: Over here!

825
00:57:51.795 --> 00:57:53.294
Clem, focus.

826
00:57:53.462 --> 00:57:56.294
I hired them, okay?
I'm sorry. I'm so stupid.

827
00:57:56.378 --> 00:57:59.377
Sweetie, calm down.
Enjoy the scenery.

828
00:57:59.587 --> 00:58:03.043
I need it to stop
before I wake up
and don't know you anymore.

829
00:58:06.378 --> 00:58:08.377
Just tell them
to cancel it then.

830
00:58:09.003 --> 00:58:10.586
What the hell are you
talking about?

831
00:58:10.753 --> 00:58:12.377
I can't just cancel it.
I'm asleep.

832
00:58:13.211 --> 00:58:14.627
Wake yourself up!

833
00:58:14.712 --> 00:58:16.794
Okay, you want me to wake up?
All right.

834
00:58:16.878 --> 00:58:19.252
Okay, here we go.
Will it make you happy
if I try?

835
00:58:19.336 --> 00:58:20.960
Yeah.
I'll try really hard.

836
00:58:21.044 --> 00:58:23.502
Here we go.
That was a great idea.

837
00:58:26.211 --> 00:58:28.419
That's working
like gangbusters.

838
00:58:29.211 --> 00:58:31.544
MARY: Don't!
That tickles me!

839
00:58:33.128 --> 00:58:35.669
STAN: What the hell is that?
It's a birthmark!

840
00:58:38.878 --> 00:58:40.877
It did work, for a second.

841
00:58:42.211 --> 00:58:43.793
But I couldn't...
See?

842
00:58:43.878 --> 00:58:45.419
I couldn't move.

843
00:58:46.587 --> 00:58:49.627
Isn't that just another one
of Joel's self-fulfilling
prophecies?

844
00:58:49.712 --> 00:58:52.252
It's more important
to prove me wrong
than to actually...

845
00:58:52.336 --> 00:58:55.252
I don't want to discuss this
right now, okay?

846
00:58:55.336 --> 00:58:56.461
Fine.

847
00:58:58.628 --> 00:59:01.751
Then what? I'm listening.

848
00:59:01.878 --> 00:59:03.960
I don't know.
You erased me.

849
00:59:04.044 --> 00:59:06.627
That's why I'm here
and doing this.

850
00:59:06.752 --> 00:59:10.544
I'm sorry.
You know me, I'm impulsive.

851
00:59:14.836 --> 00:59:17.043
That's what I love about you.

852
00:59:23.170 --> 00:59:25.711
CLEMENTINE:
I have another idea
for this problem.

853
00:59:25.878 --> 00:59:27.627
This is a memory of me.

854
00:59:27.712 --> 00:59:30.127
The way you wanted
to have sex on the couch

855
00:59:30.211 --> 00:59:32.586
after you look down
at my crotch.

856
00:59:33.961 --> 00:59:36.085
The eraser guys are coming,

857
00:59:36.462 --> 00:59:38.502
so what if you take me
somewhere else,

858
00:59:38.587 --> 00:59:40.294
somewhere where
I don't belong,

859
00:59:40.712 --> 00:59:42.169
and we hide there
till morning?

860
00:59:49.211 --> 00:59:51.461
I can't remember anything
without you.

861
00:59:52.670 --> 00:59:55.377
That's very sweet,
but try, okay?
Okay.

862
01:00:04.003 --> 01:00:08.043
Row, row, row your boat
Gently down the stream

863
01:00:09.003 --> 01:00:12.627
Merrily, merrily,
merrily, merrily
Life is but a dream

864
01:00:21.378 --> 01:00:24.668
CLEMENTINE: It's working.
I'm a genius.

865
01:00:52.752 --> 01:00:54.377
Where did you go?

866
01:00:55.003 --> 01:00:56.960
I'm supposed to come, too!

867
01:00:57.044 --> 01:00:58.586
WOMAN: I'm just gonna go
get a salad bowl.

868
01:00:58.669 --> 01:01:00.377
Can you stir the soup
and keep an eye on Joel?

869
01:01:00.462 --> 01:01:02.002
He likes to be near me.

870
01:01:02.086 --> 01:01:03.835
CLEMENTINE:
Absolutely.

871
01:01:04.420 --> 01:01:08.002
It worked.
My God, look at this.

872
01:01:08.878 --> 01:01:10.751
It worked!

873
01:01:11.420 --> 01:01:12.960
Look at this dress, man.

874
01:01:14.711 --> 01:01:15.918
I wish I could
take it with me.

875
01:01:18.462 --> 01:01:20.586
Who am I?
Mrs. Hamlyn.

876
01:01:20.711 --> 01:01:21.835
Right. Mrs. Hamlyn.

877
01:01:21.919 --> 01:01:24.586
I must be about four.
Oh, my gosh.

878
01:01:25.003 --> 01:01:28.210
Found the salad bowl.
I'm serving salad
and string beans.

879
01:01:28.295 --> 01:01:31.127
Is he okay under there?
Honey, are you all right?

880
01:01:31.211 --> 01:01:33.419
I feel like
I could clean up all day.

881
01:01:33.503 --> 01:01:36.335
Would you hate me
if I asked you to clean
some string beans?

882
01:01:36.420 --> 01:01:39.544
No, not at all.
God, I love this kitchen.

883
01:01:39.878 --> 01:01:41.544
Thank you so much.

884
01:01:41.961 --> 01:01:44.502
She's not looking at me.
She's busy.

885
01:01:46.503 --> 01:01:49.710
No one ever looks at me.
I want my mommy.

886
01:01:49.961 --> 01:01:51.461
CLEMENTINE:
Oh, baby Joel.

887
01:01:52.711 --> 01:01:54.710
JOEL'S MOTHER:
Is every little peanut
under there okay?

888
01:01:54.794 --> 01:01:56.085
He's fine.

889
01:01:56.170 --> 01:01:57.877
Do you have
something to drink?

890
01:01:57.961 --> 01:02:00.419
JOEL'S MOTHER:
How about a cocktail?
I know it's not 5:00...

891
01:02:00.503 --> 01:02:01.626
I would die for a vodka.

892
01:02:01.711 --> 01:02:03.210
Let me check
if I have that.

893
01:02:03.295 --> 01:02:05.043
Okay, I'm just going
to wait right here.

894
01:02:05.128 --> 01:02:08.127
No, sweetie. Joely?

895
01:02:08.211 --> 01:02:11.377
Your mother
wants me to mind you.
Get back under the table.

896
01:02:11.462 --> 01:02:12.502
Ice cream.

897
01:02:12.586 --> 01:02:16.294
No, not until
after you've had your dinner.

898
01:02:16.378 --> 01:02:19.960
Come on! Grow up.

899
01:02:20.086 --> 01:02:21.626
JOEL:
Don't leave me, Clem.
Oh, my God.

900
01:02:21.711 --> 01:02:24.127
No, I'm right here.
This is sort of warped.

901
01:02:24.211 --> 01:02:26.793
I'm scared.
I want my mommy.

902
01:02:26.878 --> 01:02:30.043
Don't cry, baby Joel.
It's okay.

903
01:02:32.420 --> 01:02:36.252
Joel, stop it!
I think it's working.
We're hidden, Joel. Look!

904
01:02:36.711 --> 01:02:38.002
Honey, look.

905
01:02:39.044 --> 01:02:40.252
Wait there.

906
01:02:44.253 --> 01:02:47.626
My crotch is still here,
just as you remembered it.

907
01:02:47.794 --> 01:02:48.751
Yuck.

908
01:02:48.752 --> 01:02:48.877
Yuck.

909
01:02:53.336 --> 01:02:55.585
It stopped.
What?

910
01:02:56.711 --> 01:02:58.419
It stopped erasing.

911
01:02:58.836 --> 01:03:02.543
Oh, shit!
This is terrible.

912
01:03:05.211 --> 01:03:07.335
He's off the map.

913
01:03:07.420 --> 01:03:10.877
MARY: Where?
I don't know where.

914
01:03:11.211 --> 01:03:14.960
This is very bad news.
Where are my glasses?

915
01:03:16.878 --> 01:03:20.877
Crap! What did we do?
What do I do?

916
01:03:21.003 --> 01:03:23.461
What shall we do?
STAN:
I don't know what to do.

917
01:03:23.544 --> 01:03:26.793
What shall we do?
I just said, I don't know.

918
01:03:26.878 --> 01:03:28.461
I'm sorry.
What shall we do?

919
01:03:28.544 --> 01:03:31.751
I don't know. Mellow out.
You're freaking me out.

920
01:03:31.836 --> 01:03:35.877
We have to do something.
He could wake up
all half-baked.

921
01:03:36.003 --> 01:03:40.210
Quiet.
You're freaking me out.
All gooey and half-baked.

922
01:03:41.170 --> 01:03:43.918
That sounds so good.
I'm hungry.

923
01:03:44.086 --> 01:03:46.626
Oh, shit. What?

924
01:03:48.211 --> 01:03:49.751
We should call Howard.

925
01:03:49.836 --> 01:03:53.626
No way. No sir, man.
This is my...
I can handle this.

926
01:03:53.711 --> 01:03:55.585
You can't call Howard.

927
01:03:57.128 --> 01:03:58.960
There's no time
to fuck around.

928
01:03:59.044 --> 01:04:01.294
I've got this under control.
What are you talking about?

929
01:04:01.378 --> 01:04:02.501
Stop fucking around.

930
01:04:02.586 --> 01:04:03.751
Okay. I'll call Howard.

931
01:04:11.878 --> 01:04:12.918
Hello?

932
01:04:13.003 --> 01:04:17.335
Howard, it's Stan.
I'm working on this guy
down here.

933
01:04:17.420 --> 01:04:19.043
We've lost him
for a moment,

934
01:04:19.878 --> 01:04:22.294
and I can't
bring him back up.

935
01:04:22.378 --> 01:04:25.918
Okay, tell me what happened
before he disappeared.

936
01:04:26.003 --> 01:04:29.294
I wasn't sure
because I was away
from the monitor for a minute,

937
01:04:29.378 --> 01:04:33.169
and I had it on auto-pilot
because I had to pee.

938
01:04:33.253 --> 01:04:34.918
DR. MIERZWIAK:
Where was Patrick?

939
01:04:35.044 --> 01:04:37.585
He had to go home sick.

940
01:04:40.544 --> 01:04:41.626
What's the address?

941
01:04:41.711 --> 01:04:42.751
STAN: I know,
I'm so sorry.

942
01:04:42.836 --> 01:04:44.002
That's okay. Come on.

943
01:04:44.086 --> 01:04:46.252
We're at 159 South Village.

944
01:04:46.586 --> 01:04:49.377
Apartment 1-E.
Rockville Center.

945
01:04:49.502 --> 01:04:51.668
Mary, he's coming right now.

946
01:04:51.878 --> 01:04:52.877
MARY: I'm staying.

947
01:04:54.044 --> 01:04:56.043
Get your stuff, Mary.

948
01:04:56.544 --> 01:04:57.877
I think you should go.

949
01:04:58.211 --> 01:04:59.252
No.

950
01:05:02.878 --> 01:05:04.460
I am so stoned.

951
01:05:04.544 --> 01:05:07.626
STAN: Please, Mary,
you have to go.

952
01:05:07.711 --> 01:05:11.085
Stop being stoned.
I don't want him
to see me stoned.

953
01:05:12.044 --> 01:05:16.127
You have no idea
how much trouble I'll get into
if Howard comes...

954
01:05:16.419 --> 01:05:19.294
CLEMENTINE: Joel, stop. Look.

955
01:05:25.711 --> 01:05:29.710
I want her to pick me up.
Weird how strong
that desire is.

956
01:05:29.794 --> 01:05:32.960
Joel, look at me.
You'll remember me
in the morning,

957
01:05:33.044 --> 01:05:36.877
you'll come to me,
you'll tell me about us,
and we'll start over.

958
01:05:38.336 --> 01:05:41.418
Pat? I thought we could
have a little cocktail.

959
01:05:41.502 --> 01:05:44.210
That Patrick guy,
he's copying me.

960
01:05:44.295 --> 01:05:45.751
What Patrick guy?

961
01:05:45.919 --> 01:05:47.626
That guy.
What?

962
01:05:47.711 --> 01:05:49.751
He's here, in my apartment.

963
01:05:49.836 --> 01:05:53.043
One of the eraser guys.
He fell for you
when they were doing you,

964
01:05:53.128 --> 01:05:57.085
and now
he's introduced himself
like he doesn't even know you,

965
01:05:57.461 --> 01:05:59.668
and you guys are dating.
Really?

966
01:06:00.669 --> 01:06:01.793
Is he cute?

967
01:06:04.295 --> 01:06:06.418
There's nothing wrong
with you.

968
01:06:06.502 --> 01:06:09.543
You're the most wonderful
person I've ever met.

969
01:06:10.752 --> 01:06:13.710
You're kind, beautiful,

970
01:06:14.836 --> 01:06:19.127
smart, funny, and nice.

971
01:06:20.253 --> 01:06:21.294
What?

972
01:06:22.961 --> 01:06:24.543
Okay, all right.

973
01:06:29.253 --> 01:06:31.835
Move. Come on,
let's go.
Careful.

974
01:06:33.836 --> 01:06:35.543
I'm still stoned.

975
01:06:36.794 --> 01:06:39.585
Those eye drops
you gave me didn't do shit.

976
01:06:44.335 --> 01:06:45.626
Be cool.

977
01:06:50.377 --> 01:06:52.210
Hello, Mary,
what are you doing here?

978
01:06:52.294 --> 01:06:54.002
STAN: Hi, Howard.
She was just here
to help out.

979
01:06:54.086 --> 01:06:57.334
I wanted to understand
as much about the procedure
as possible.

980
01:06:57.544 --> 01:07:01.751
I think it's important
for my job to understand
the inner workings

981
01:07:01.836 --> 01:07:03.460
of the work that we do.

982
01:07:03.544 --> 01:07:06.835
Not that I do,
but the work that is done

983
01:07:06.919 --> 01:07:08.793
by people where I also work.

984
01:07:08.878 --> 01:07:10.418
The work of my colleagues.

985
01:07:11.627 --> 01:07:15.418
Let's see if we can
get to the bottom of this,
shall we?

986
01:07:21.086 --> 01:07:22.127
That's odd.

987
01:07:22.211 --> 01:07:23.668
I already tried that.

988
01:07:23.752 --> 01:07:24.960
You tried going through
the C-gate?

989
01:07:25.044 --> 01:07:26.877
Of course.

990
01:07:27.128 --> 01:07:29.169
I mean, yes.

991
01:07:33.836 --> 01:07:35.210
All right.

992
01:07:37.502 --> 01:07:39.877
You want to get linked up?
Yeah.

993
01:07:42.003 --> 01:07:45.793
I ran the utility programs,
and I had nothing there,

994
01:07:45.878 --> 01:07:49.334
so I checked all the memories
against the printed logs.

995
01:07:49.461 --> 01:07:52.626
Here, Howard,
I got you a chair.
Thank you.

996
01:07:52.711 --> 01:07:54.877
There you go.
You're welcome.

997
01:07:55.878 --> 01:07:57.376
All right.
I've got it.

998
01:07:57.461 --> 01:08:00.210
I'll go through
the entire memory,

999
01:08:00.544 --> 01:08:01.543
see if something
comes up.

1000
01:08:09.003 --> 01:08:11.002
I love being bathed
in the sink.

1001
01:08:11.294 --> 01:08:13.085
Such a feeling of security.

1002
01:08:14.128 --> 01:08:16.543
I've never seen you happier,
baby Joel.

1003
01:08:17.461 --> 01:08:18.877
DR. MIERZWIAK:
There it is.

1004
01:08:19.170 --> 01:08:22.460
I don't understand
why it's off the map
like that.

1005
01:08:24.128 --> 01:08:26.002
What the heck
was he doing there?

1006
01:08:35.252 --> 01:08:36.626
His eyes are open.

1007
01:08:39.210 --> 01:08:41.918
Has this happened before
with him?
No.

1008
01:08:42.961 --> 01:08:45.376
This is not good.

1009
01:08:48.752 --> 01:08:51.251
I'm going to have
to give him this.

1010
01:09:15.044 --> 01:09:17.918
WOMAN ON SCREEN:
Can't you see
I love you, Antoine?

1011
01:09:18.794 --> 01:09:20.543
DR. MIERZWIAK:
Okay, we're back in.

1012
01:09:22.836 --> 01:09:27.710
That was beautiful to watch,
Howard, like a surgeon
or a concert pianist.

1013
01:09:30.086 --> 01:09:31.710
Thank you, Mary.

1014
01:09:32.461 --> 01:09:35.710
Howard, you should
get some sleep.
I think I'll be fine now.

1015
01:09:35.794 --> 01:09:39.418
Can't you see I love you,
Antoine?

1016
01:09:40.961 --> 01:09:43.668
Lucky me. Lay one on me.

1017
01:09:48.335 --> 01:09:51.543
Don't call me Antoine.
My name is Wally.

1018
01:09:51.627 --> 01:09:55.085
Yes, I know, but how can
a woman love a man
with a name like Wally?

1019
01:09:56.294 --> 01:09:57.751
What was that?

1020
01:09:57.878 --> 01:10:00.460
My God, there's people
coming out of your butt.

1021
01:10:00.544 --> 01:10:01.793
There is?

1022
01:10:04.210 --> 01:10:05.293
Got it.

1023
01:10:05.627 --> 01:10:09.501
Tangerine! Come on.
We've got to go.

1024
01:10:09.586 --> 01:10:11.793
Go on. Please go.

1025
01:10:14.919 --> 01:10:17.043
STAN: You can run,
but you can't hide.

1026
01:10:17.586 --> 01:10:18.960
JOEL:
Clem, come on!

1027
01:10:19.961 --> 01:10:20.960
JOEL: There I am.

1028
01:10:22.919 --> 01:10:24.084
That truck.

1029
01:10:24.169 --> 01:10:26.877
Doc? Please!

1030
01:10:28.502 --> 01:10:33.251
Let's begin by
you telling me everything
you remember...

1031
01:10:34.210 --> 01:10:37.460
That's strange.
He's in a memory
that we've already erased.

1032
01:10:39.127 --> 01:10:42.460
At least we know where he is.
He's back on track, right?

1033
01:10:42.794 --> 01:10:43.960
Come on, Clem.

1034
01:10:44.044 --> 01:10:46.751
STAN: He's developed
some sort of resistance
to the procedure.

1035
01:10:46.836 --> 01:10:48.668
I don't want to run anymore.

1036
01:10:49.210 --> 01:10:50.209
Shit.

1037
01:10:51.794 --> 01:10:53.002
Come on.

1038
01:10:53.085 --> 01:10:55.460
Hide me somewhere deeper,
somewhere really buried.

1039
01:10:55.544 --> 01:10:58.209
Where?
Hide me in your humiliation.

1040
01:10:59.294 --> 01:11:00.334
Humiliation.

1041
01:11:00.419 --> 01:11:02.293
BOY: Come on, you big baby.

1042
01:11:10.836 --> 01:11:11.877
No!

1043
01:11:13.210 --> 01:11:15.418
MARY: Bye, Howard.
Wait.

1044
01:11:16.752 --> 01:11:18.376
He's disappeared again.

1045
01:11:18.544 --> 01:11:19.960
Oh, dear.

1046
01:11:21.627 --> 01:11:23.126
MARY: I'm so sorry, Howard.

1047
01:11:23.711 --> 01:11:25.084
JOEL: Humiliation.

1048
01:11:31.419 --> 01:11:35.376
I don't like it, either.
I'm trying to find
horrible secret places to...

1049
01:11:35.461 --> 01:11:37.460
Honey, I have a surprise.

1050
01:11:39.002 --> 01:11:41.418
You know what?
I'll just ask you
in the morning.

1051
01:11:42.502 --> 01:11:43.501
Good night.

1052
01:11:47.544 --> 01:11:49.710
I'm sorry.
JOEL: Shut up.

1053
01:11:51.252 --> 01:11:52.460
Look.

1054
01:11:54.669 --> 01:11:57.710
Joel, look where we are.

1055
01:12:01.878 --> 01:12:03.126
This isn't good.

1056
01:12:03.210 --> 01:12:06.877
Then hide me somewhere
really buried.

1057
01:12:07.961 --> 01:12:10.001
BOYS: Hit it, Joel!

1058
01:12:10.085 --> 01:12:14.376
JOEL: I can't,
I've got to go home.
I'll do it later!

1059
01:12:34.043 --> 01:12:35.793
BOY: He has a girlfriend.

1060
01:12:35.878 --> 01:12:39.835
Wait, what am I doing?
Freddy, you don't
scare me anymore.

1061
01:12:42.960 --> 01:12:45.293
Joely, get up.
Come on, it's not worth it.

1062
01:12:45.377 --> 01:12:47.460
They're not worth it, Joel.

1063
01:12:48.836 --> 01:12:50.501
He's not listening!
Come on.

1064
01:12:50.586 --> 01:12:52.001
Stupid!

1065
01:12:58.544 --> 01:13:00.293
JOEL: I'm so ashamed.

1066
01:13:00.377 --> 01:13:04.959
CLEMENTINE: It's okay.
You were a little kid.
Come on.

1067
01:13:05.169 --> 01:13:07.042
That's where I live, lived.

1068
01:13:07.294 --> 01:13:09.168
I wish I knew you
when I was a kid.

1069
01:13:09.252 --> 01:13:11.710
Do you like my pink hat?
Here, look, feel better.

1070
01:13:11.794 --> 01:13:14.084
You can really kill me
this time. It's my turn. Go.

1071
01:13:14.169 --> 01:13:16.710
You're really going to die,
though, okay?

1072
01:13:16.794 --> 01:13:18.126
One, two, three.

1073
01:13:18.210 --> 01:13:19.460
You're dead.

1074
01:13:21.043 --> 01:13:22.418
My mom.

1075
01:13:22.669 --> 01:13:25.793
It's okay, we're playing.
It's not real.

1076
01:13:25.878 --> 01:13:27.042
He's killing me.

1077
01:13:27.127 --> 01:13:30.126
Are you dead yet?
You're dead!

1078
01:13:31.627 --> 01:13:34.460
I think
I got the hang of this.
I still don't understand it,

1079
01:13:34.544 --> 01:13:36.543
but I'm finding him
quickly enough.

1080
01:14:14.335 --> 01:14:15.793
Are you okay?

1081
01:14:19.877 --> 01:14:24.042
Oh, my God, that was terrible.
Almost three seconds.

1082
01:14:24.544 --> 01:14:25.751
JOEL:
Let's do it one more time.

1083
01:14:25.877 --> 01:14:27.376
One more
and then I get to go.

1084
01:14:41.960 --> 01:14:43.168
This is so cool!

1085
01:14:43.252 --> 01:14:45.084
Look out!

1086
01:14:49.169 --> 01:14:50.543
It's fluff.

1087
01:14:51.877 --> 01:14:53.293
Our house.

1088
01:14:58.544 --> 01:15:00.501
Wait, we've got to go.

1089
01:15:02.711 --> 01:15:04.251
Come on.

1090
01:15:12.169 --> 01:15:14.543
This is a really bad time
for this.

1091
01:15:16.711 --> 01:15:18.585
I don't even know
where we're going.

1092
01:15:18.669 --> 01:15:21.126
It's going to be fun.
It's the best place.

1093
01:15:21.210 --> 01:15:24.001
No, this way.
This way. Come on.

1094
01:15:24.877 --> 01:15:26.710
You're no help at all.

1095
01:15:28.669 --> 01:15:29.876
Come on.

1096
01:15:30.544 --> 01:15:32.334
Let go of me, Joel.

1097
01:15:45.711 --> 01:15:47.792
I like watching you work,
Howard.

1098
01:15:52.252 --> 01:15:56.501
I guess I'll go out
for some air,

1099
01:15:56.960 --> 01:15:58.376
if nobody minds.

1100
01:15:58.751 --> 01:16:02.126
It looks like
you have everything
under control here.

1101
01:16:02.419 --> 01:16:05.168
Yeah, that's fine.

1102
01:16:16.461 --> 01:16:18.585
MARY:
Do you like quotes, Howard?

1103
01:16:20.210 --> 01:16:21.418
What do you mean?

1104
01:16:21.502 --> 01:16:23.668
Like famous quotes.

1105
01:16:24.627 --> 01:16:26.917
I find reading them
inspirational,

1106
01:16:27.002 --> 01:16:31.876
and in my reading,
I've come across some
I thought you might like, too.

1107
01:16:32.918 --> 01:16:34.501
I'd love to hear some.

1108
01:16:34.586 --> 01:16:37.626
There's one that goes,
"Blessed are the forgetful,

1109
01:16:37.710 --> 01:16:40.626
"for they get the better
even of their blunders."

1110
01:16:40.710 --> 01:16:42.460
That's Nietzsche, right?
Yeah.

1111
01:16:42.544 --> 01:16:44.834
I thought I could tell you
something you didn't know.

1112
01:16:44.918 --> 01:16:48.876
No, it's a good quote.
I'm happy we both know it.

1113
01:16:50.710 --> 01:16:52.251
There's this
other one I like.

1114
01:16:52.335 --> 01:16:54.042
It's by Pope Alexander
and it goes...

1115
01:16:54.793 --> 01:16:56.418
Alexander Pope?

1116
01:16:56.502 --> 01:16:58.376
Oh, yeah. Shit.

1117
01:16:59.002 --> 01:17:02.543
It's just that I told myself
not to say "Pope Alexander"

1118
01:17:02.627 --> 01:17:05.168
and sound like a dope,
and then I go ahead
and say it.

1119
01:17:05.252 --> 01:17:08.209
It's no big deal.
You're such a sweetheart.

1120
01:17:10.668 --> 01:17:14.293
The quote goes, "How happy
is the blameless vestal's lot!

1121
01:17:15.793 --> 01:17:18.585
MARY: "The world forgetting
by the world forgot

1122
01:17:19.668 --> 01:17:22.126
"Eternal sunshine
of the spotless mind!

1123
01:17:23.210 --> 01:17:26.959
"Each pray'r accepted
and each wish resign'd"

1124
01:17:27.043 --> 01:17:31.460
I want to be a great,
big, huge elephant.

1125
01:17:32.461 --> 01:17:34.709
With a huge trunk like that.

1126
01:17:39.043 --> 01:17:41.667
I haven't heard that one.
It's lovely.

1127
01:17:42.043 --> 01:17:44.667
I just thought
it would be appropriate,
maybe.

1128
01:17:49.668 --> 01:17:52.001
I really admire
the work you do.

1129
01:17:53.461 --> 01:17:54.667
I don't mean to be
so familiar...

1130
01:17:54.751 --> 01:17:57.834
It's fine.
I'm happy to hear...

1131
01:18:04.210 --> 01:18:05.585
I'm sorry.

1132
01:18:09.544 --> 01:18:12.084
I've loved you
for a very long time.

1133
01:18:14.877 --> 01:18:16.543
I shouldn't have said that.

1134
01:18:16.626 --> 01:18:19.625
Mary, you're
a wonderful girl.

1135
01:18:22.169 --> 01:18:24.876
But, you know,
I have a wife and kids.

1136
01:18:30.585 --> 01:18:33.126
Mary, we can't do this.

1137
01:18:49.710 --> 01:18:51.917
Good morning,
Mrs. Mierzwiak.

1138
01:19:01.544 --> 01:19:03.584
MARY: What? Who is it?
DR. MIERZWIAK: Oh, my God.

1139
01:19:17.377 --> 01:19:19.460
Thank you, Stan.
Thanks a lot.

1140
01:19:24.877 --> 01:19:26.917
Hollis!

1141
01:19:30.377 --> 01:19:31.501
Wait.

1142
01:19:33.419 --> 01:19:34.876
I knew it, Howard.

1143
01:19:34.960 --> 01:19:37.334
It didn't start out like this.
I came here to work.

1144
01:19:37.419 --> 01:19:39.625
This is a one-time mistake.

1145
01:19:39.710 --> 01:19:41.792
I'm a stupid girl
with a crush.

1146
01:19:41.877 --> 01:19:44.209
I basically
forced him into it.

1147
01:19:45.585 --> 01:19:48.042
Don't be a monster.
Tell the girl.

1148
01:19:51.169 --> 01:19:52.625
Tell me what?

1149
01:19:53.210 --> 01:19:54.876
Oh, you poor kid.

1150
01:19:56.710 --> 01:19:59.792
You can have him.
You did.

1151
01:20:10.793 --> 01:20:11.876
What?

1152
01:20:22.169 --> 01:20:23.834
We have a history.

1153
01:20:25.877 --> 01:20:28.959
I'm sorry.
You wanted the procedure.

1154
01:20:30.960 --> 01:20:35.542
You wanted it done
so you could get past...

1155
01:20:43.210 --> 01:20:47.667
I have to
finish the work in there.
It's almost morning.

1156
01:20:49.835 --> 01:20:53.293
We'll talk later, okay?

1157
01:21:11.835 --> 01:21:13.959
Let me give you a lift home.

1158
01:21:29.543 --> 01:21:33.001
Didn't figure you'd show
your face around me again.

1159
01:21:33.877 --> 01:21:36.876
I thought you were humiliated.

1160
01:21:37.043 --> 01:21:38.792
You did run away,
after all.

1161
01:21:39.460 --> 01:21:41.293
JOEL:
I just needed to see you.

1162
01:21:41.377 --> 01:21:42.459
Yeah?

1163
01:21:44.085 --> 01:21:45.750
I'd like to

1164
01:21:46.835 --> 01:21:48.625
take you out or something.

1165
01:21:50.043 --> 01:21:51.542
You're married.

1166
01:21:52.294 --> 01:21:54.500
Not yet. Not married.

1167
01:21:55.460 --> 01:21:57.168
No, I'm not married.

1168
01:21:57.335 --> 01:22:00.876
Look, I'm telling you
right off the bat,
I'm high maintenance,

1169
01:22:00.960 --> 01:22:04.625
so I'm not gonna tiptoe
around your marriage

1170
01:22:04.710 --> 01:22:06.959
or whatever it is
you've got going there.

1171
01:22:07.043 --> 01:22:09.876
If you want to be with me,
you're with me.

1172
01:22:10.376 --> 01:22:11.459
Okay.

1173
01:22:12.169 --> 01:22:15.625
Too many guys think
I'm a concept,
or I complete them

1174
01:22:15.710 --> 01:22:18.001
or I'm gonna make them alive.

1175
01:22:18.585 --> 01:22:22.126
I'm just a fucked-up girl
who's looking for
my own peace of mind.

1176
01:22:22.210 --> 01:22:23.584
Don't assign me yours.

1177
01:22:23.668 --> 01:22:25.959
I remember that speech
really well.

1178
01:22:27.002 --> 01:22:28.542
I had you pegged,
didn't I?

1179
01:22:28.626 --> 01:22:30.584
Had the whole human race
pegged.

1180
01:22:31.335 --> 01:22:32.584
Probably.

1181
01:22:34.585 --> 01:22:36.709
I still thought
you were going
to save my life.

1182
01:22:37.043 --> 01:22:38.042
Even after that.

1183
01:22:40.294 --> 01:22:41.542
I know.

1184
01:22:44.460 --> 01:22:46.417
It would be different,

1185
01:22:47.877 --> 01:22:50.500
if we could just
give it another go-round.

1186
01:22:54.127 --> 01:22:57.667
Remember me.
Try your best.

1187
01:23:01.210 --> 01:23:02.667
Maybe we can.

1188
01:23:34.460 --> 01:23:37.209
DR. MIERZWIAK:
Just tell me
what you remember,

1189
01:23:37.293 --> 01:23:38.917
and we'll take it
from there.

1190
01:23:42.210 --> 01:23:44.251
MARY:
I liked you immediately.

1191
01:23:45.127 --> 01:23:48.625
You didn't come on to me
at all. I liked that.

1192
01:23:51.127 --> 01:23:53.625
I was so tongue-tied
around you at first,

1193
01:23:53.710 --> 01:23:56.333
but I wanted you to think
I was smart.

1194
01:23:57.793 --> 01:23:59.959
I couldn't wait
to come to work.

1195
01:24:00.043 --> 01:24:04.542
I had these fantasies
of us being married
and having kids...

1196
01:24:07.127 --> 01:24:09.042
Howie, I can't do this.

1197
01:24:09.877 --> 01:24:11.959
We agreed
it's for the best, Mary.

1198
01:24:12.043 --> 01:24:13.292
Yeah, I know.

1199
01:24:15.251 --> 01:24:16.542
Oh, God!

1200
01:24:17.002 --> 01:24:19.292
CARRIE: I'll take the bottom
and you...

1201
01:24:19.376 --> 01:24:21.333
No, Joel,
help me with that.

1202
01:24:21.418 --> 01:24:22.542
Will you get the cooler?

1203
01:24:22.626 --> 01:24:24.292
Honey, the cooler's pretty...

1204
01:24:24.376 --> 01:24:25.667
She can get it.

1205
01:24:26.501 --> 01:24:28.333
Let me get that.
No, no, no.

1206
01:24:28.418 --> 01:24:29.459
Don't take anything.

1207
01:24:29.543 --> 01:24:30.667
I can take the plane.

1208
01:24:30.751 --> 01:24:33.084
Put the gate back up.

1209
01:24:36.376 --> 01:24:38.250
JOEL: This is the day we met.

1210
01:24:38.501 --> 01:24:41.959
You were by the surf.
I could just make you out
in the distance.

1211
01:24:42.043 --> 01:24:44.625
I remember being drawn to you,
even then.

1212
01:24:44.710 --> 01:24:46.876
I thought,
"Wow, how odd!

1213
01:24:46.960 --> 01:24:48.959
"I'm drawn to someone's back."

1214
01:24:49.209 --> 01:24:51.292
You were
in that orange sweatshirt

1215
01:24:51.376 --> 01:24:55.001
that I would
come to know so well,
and even hate, eventually.

1216
01:24:55.543 --> 01:24:59.625
But at the time I thought,
"How cool,
an orange sweatshirt."

1217
01:24:59.710 --> 01:25:01.042
Hi, there.

1218
01:25:03.293 --> 01:25:04.417
Hi.

1219
01:25:04.501 --> 01:25:08.208
I saw you sitting over here
by yourself,

1220
01:25:09.501 --> 01:25:12.168
and I thought,
"Thank God,

1221
01:25:12.376 --> 01:25:15.959
"someone normal who
doesn't know how to interact
at these things."

1222
01:25:17.543 --> 01:25:20.126
I don't ever know
what to say.

1223
01:25:20.751 --> 01:25:22.292
I'm Clementine.

1224
01:25:23.460 --> 01:25:26.333
Can I borrow
a piece of your chicken?

1225
01:25:27.209 --> 01:25:30.417
And then you just took it,
without waiting for an answer.

1226
01:25:35.043 --> 01:25:38.792
It was so intimate,
like we were already lovers.

1227
01:25:41.418 --> 01:25:42.709
I'm Joel.

1228
01:25:43.751 --> 01:25:47.500
Hi, Joel.
So, no jokes about my name.

1229
01:25:49.209 --> 01:25:50.208
You mean, like

1230
01:25:50.293 --> 01:25:52.959
"Oh, my darlin', Clementine?"

1231
01:25:53.543 --> 01:25:56.001
Huckleberry Hound?
That sort of thing?

1232
01:25:56.085 --> 01:25:58.292
Yeah, like that.

1233
01:25:58.376 --> 01:25:59.917
No, no jokes.

1234
01:26:00.293 --> 01:26:02.375
One of my favorite things
when I was a kid

1235
01:26:02.460 --> 01:26:04.709
was my Huckleberry Hound doll.

1236
01:26:08.168 --> 01:26:10.375
I think your name is magical.

1237
01:26:13.376 --> 01:26:16.876
This is it, Joel.
It's gonna be gone soon.

1238
01:26:19.793 --> 01:26:20.959
I know.

1239
01:26:22.376 --> 01:26:23.876
What do we do?

1240
01:26:26.835 --> 01:26:28.084
Enjoy it.

1241
01:26:45.710 --> 01:26:47.542
CLEMENTINE: You married?
JOEL: No.

1242
01:26:47.793 --> 01:26:50.042
Let's move into
this neighborhood!

1243
01:26:50.126 --> 01:26:52.667
I do sort of live
with someone, though.

1244
01:26:53.209 --> 01:26:54.625
Male or female?

1245
01:26:54.710 --> 01:26:57.208
What? Female.

1246
01:27:00.960 --> 01:27:03.792
At least I'm not barking up
the wrong tree.

1247
01:27:07.043 --> 01:27:08.959
Do you know these people?

1248
01:27:09.043 --> 01:27:10.542
No, of course not.
Come on.

1249
01:27:12.960 --> 01:27:14.459
They might have a dog.

1250
01:27:14.543 --> 01:27:15.876
There's no dog.

1251
01:27:17.877 --> 01:27:19.876
What are you doing?

1252
01:27:19.960 --> 01:27:21.375
It's freezing out.

1253
01:27:22.334 --> 01:27:24.125
I don't believe this.

1254
01:27:36.334 --> 01:27:38.709
Come on, man.
The water's fine.

1255
01:27:40.168 --> 01:27:42.876
Nobody's coming here tonight,
believe me.

1256
01:27:47.376 --> 01:27:51.041
So, what's
your girlfriend's name?

1257
01:27:52.209 --> 01:27:54.584
Naomi,
but we're not really...

1258
01:27:55.877 --> 01:27:58.667
Whatever.
So this is great.

1259
01:27:58.751 --> 01:28:03.625
Now I can look
for candles, matches,
and the liquor cabinet.

1260
01:28:03.835 --> 01:28:05.041
Oh, God.

1261
01:28:12.042 --> 01:28:13.167
I think we should go.

1262
01:28:13.251 --> 01:28:15.041
There's no phone line.

1263
01:28:15.460 --> 01:28:17.292
What?
I think we should go.

1264
01:28:17.376 --> 01:28:21.041
Why? It's our house.
Just for tonight.

1265
01:28:21.126 --> 01:28:24.250
We are
David and Ruth Laskin.

1266
01:28:25.668 --> 01:28:27.459
Which one do you want to be?

1267
01:28:27.668 --> 01:28:30.750
I prefer to be Ruth,
but I can be flexible.

1268
01:28:33.084 --> 01:28:34.542
What do you need?

1269
01:28:36.334 --> 01:28:37.500
Alcohol.

1270
01:28:39.501 --> 01:28:41.000
So, are you okay with wine?

1271
01:28:41.084 --> 01:28:42.208
I don't know.

1272
01:28:42.293 --> 01:28:43.917
Well, you choose the wine.

1273
01:28:44.001 --> 01:28:47.959
I'll go find the bedroom
and slip into
something more Ruth.

1274
01:28:51.460 --> 01:28:54.375
I'm Ruth-less at the moment.
JOEL: We really should go.

1275
01:28:56.710 --> 01:28:58.709
I've got to catch my ride.

1276
01:29:00.877 --> 01:29:02.333
CLEMENTINE: So go.

1277
01:29:03.418 --> 01:29:07.375
I did. I thought
maybe you were a nut.

1278
01:29:08.710 --> 01:29:10.417
But you were exciting.

1279
01:29:12.668 --> 01:29:14.417
I wish you'd stayed.

1280
01:29:14.501 --> 01:29:17.459
I wish I'd stayed, too.
Now I wish I'd stayed.

1281
01:29:17.543 --> 01:29:19.876
I wish I'd done
a lot of things.

1282
01:29:26.918 --> 01:29:29.709
I wish I'd stayed. I do.

1283
01:29:29.835 --> 01:29:32.292
CLEMENTINE:
I came back downstairs
and you were gone.

1284
01:29:32.418 --> 01:29:35.167
I walked out the door.
Why?

1285
01:29:35.251 --> 01:29:38.375
I don't know. I felt
like a scared little kid.

1286
01:29:38.959 --> 01:29:40.709
It was above my head.

1287
01:29:41.501 --> 01:29:43.459
You were scared?
Yeah.

1288
01:29:45.877 --> 01:29:48.167
I thought
you knew that about me.

1289
01:29:48.793 --> 01:29:52.417
JOEL: I ran back
to the bonfire, trying
to outrun my humiliation.

1290
01:29:53.501 --> 01:29:56.208
Was it something I said?
Yeah.

1291
01:29:59.042 --> 01:30:02.876
You said "So go"
with such disdain.

1292
01:30:04.209 --> 01:30:05.792
I'm sorry.

1293
01:30:05.877 --> 01:30:06.958
It's okay.

1294
01:30:15.209 --> 01:30:17.375
What if you stayed this time?

1295
01:30:19.917 --> 01:30:21.375
I walked out the door.

1296
01:30:23.001 --> 01:30:24.000
There's no memory left.

1297
01:30:24.543 --> 01:30:26.667
Come back
and make up a goodbye.

1298
01:30:27.876 --> 01:30:29.208
Let's pretend
we had one.

1299
01:30:40.793 --> 01:30:42.125
Bye, Joel.

1300
01:30:43.626 --> 01:30:45.041
I love you.

1301
01:30:45.585 --> 01:30:48.834
Meet me in Montauk.

1302
01:30:53.585 --> 01:30:56.500
ROB: I didn't crash the plane.
The plane crashed.

1303
01:30:58.042 --> 01:31:01.958
CARRIE: You were operating
the plane with the remote
control, and it crashed.

1304
01:31:02.042 --> 01:31:03.750
ROB: It was fucking windy.
Come on.

1305
01:31:03.834 --> 01:31:06.083
You're stoned
and you're driving.

1306
01:31:06.168 --> 01:31:09.625
The pot balances it out
and brings you back up.
That's why I smoke it.

1307
01:31:09.710 --> 01:31:12.417
If I'm going to be drinking,
then I'll smoke it.

1308
01:31:12.543 --> 01:31:17.375
It does. A medical test
was done. It's proven
on the Science Network.

1309
01:31:17.460 --> 01:31:19.125
Honey, just watch the road.

1310
01:31:19.209 --> 01:31:20.542
I can't see shit.

1311
01:31:22.501 --> 01:31:25.333
I saw you talking
to a pretty girl.

1312
01:31:25.418 --> 01:31:26.500
JOEL: She was nice.

1313
01:31:26.585 --> 01:31:28.459
ROB: Yeah, man, who was it?

1314
01:31:30.668 --> 01:31:33.750
She was just a girl.

1315
01:31:41.668 --> 01:31:42.750
Okay.

1316
01:32:19.834 --> 01:32:22.250
So I've got to
drop the van off.

1317
01:32:22.543 --> 01:32:25.459
Thanks, Stan. We'll talk.

1318
01:33:52.293 --> 01:33:53.542
You've got all your stuff,
I see.

1319
01:33:53.626 --> 01:33:54.666
That's right.

1320
01:33:54.750 --> 01:33:56.625
I take it
you're not coming back.

1321
01:33:57.042 --> 01:33:59.083
I wouldn't come back
if I was you.

1322
01:33:59.168 --> 01:34:01.375
Do you swear you didn't know?
I swear.

1323
01:34:02.709 --> 01:34:04.250
So you didn't do
the erasing?

1324
01:34:04.334 --> 01:34:06.000
Of course not. God, no.

1325
01:34:06.084 --> 01:34:08.708
And you never even suspected
we were together?

1326
01:34:09.376 --> 01:34:10.791
Once, maybe.

1327
01:34:12.834 --> 01:34:16.041
I was coming back from a job,
and you were at his car,

1328
01:34:16.251 --> 01:34:18.292
and I saw you two talking.

1329
01:34:18.834 --> 01:34:21.333
So I waved to you,
and you giggled.

1330
01:34:22.042 --> 01:34:23.584
How did I look?

1331
01:34:25.959 --> 01:34:27.542
You looked happy.

1332
01:34:28.042 --> 01:34:30.542
Happy with a secret.

1333
01:34:31.959 --> 01:34:33.459
And after that?

1334
01:34:33.543 --> 01:34:35.833
I never saw you two together
again like that,

1335
01:34:35.917 --> 01:34:39.500
so I just figured
I was imagining things.

1336
01:35:05.709 --> 01:35:09.958
I really like you, Mary Svevo.
You know that?

1337
01:35:21.501 --> 01:35:22.708
Thanks.

1338
01:35:57.667 --> 01:35:59.666
Let me get my toothbrush.

1339
01:36:14.501 --> 01:36:17.459
PATRICK ON ANSWERING MACHINE:
Where are you, Clem?
I'm worried.

1340
01:36:17.542 --> 01:36:21.041
I feel like you're mad at me
and I don't know what I did.

1341
01:36:22.209 --> 01:36:23.791
What did I do?

1342
01:36:23.876 --> 01:36:27.791
I love you so much.
I'll do anything
to make you happy.

1343
01:36:28.501 --> 01:36:31.791
Just tell me what you want
me to do, and I'll do it.

1344
01:36:32.042 --> 01:36:35.791
I'm going to stop by
this morning,
just to make sure you're okay.

1345
01:36:51.376 --> 01:36:53.916
I had a really nice time
last night.

1346
01:36:55.084 --> 01:36:56.208
Nice?

1347
01:36:56.376 --> 01:37:00.958
I had the best fucking night
of my entire fucking life
last night.

1348
01:37:01.376 --> 01:37:02.875
That's better.

1349
01:37:07.042 --> 01:37:08.333
This is weird.

1350
01:37:08.418 --> 01:37:10.875
MARY: "To all patients
of Dr. Howard Mierzwiak.

1351
01:37:10.959 --> 01:37:12.292
"My name is Mary Svevo.

1352
01:37:12.376 --> 01:37:14.458
"We've met,
but you don't remember me.

1353
01:37:14.542 --> 01:37:19.167
"I worked for a company
you hired to have
part of your memory erased.

1354
01:37:19.251 --> 01:37:22.083
"I've since decided
that this is a horrible...

1355
01:37:22.209 --> 01:37:25.916
"To correct this, I'm sending
everyone's file back to them."

1356
01:37:27.709 --> 01:37:30.083
CLEMENTINE ON TAPE: My name
is Clementine Kruczynski.

1357
01:37:30.376 --> 01:37:33.041
I'm here to erase
Joel Barish.

1358
01:37:33.542 --> 01:37:35.749
What is this?
I don't know.

1359
01:37:35.834 --> 01:37:36.958
He's boring.

1360
01:37:37.042 --> 01:37:39.875
Is that enough reason
to erase someone?

1361
01:37:40.209 --> 01:37:44.583
I've been thinking how I was
before and how I am now,
and he changed me.

1362
01:37:44.667 --> 01:37:46.541
I feel like
I'm always pissy now.

1363
01:37:46.625 --> 01:37:49.791
I don't like myself
when I'm with him.
I don't like myself anymore.

1364
01:37:49.876 --> 01:37:51.791
I can't stand
to even look at him.

1365
01:37:51.876 --> 01:37:54.416
That pathetic, wimpy,
apologetic smile.

1366
01:37:54.500 --> 01:37:56.458
That sort of
wounded puppy shit.

1367
01:37:56.542 --> 01:37:58.583
What are you doing?
I'm not doing anything.

1368
01:37:58.667 --> 01:38:00.791
The bloom is certainly
off the rose at this point.

1369
01:38:00.876 --> 01:38:03.208
Are you screwing with me?
No!

1370
01:38:03.376 --> 01:38:05.916
You are screwing with me.
Joel, I'm not!

1371
01:38:06.001 --> 01:38:07.583
You clearly are!

1372
01:38:07.917 --> 01:38:10.458
Let's just take a minute
and...

1373
01:38:39.375 --> 01:38:42.541
Patrick,
get the fuck away from me!

1374
01:38:43.542 --> 01:38:46.292
Can we talk about it?
CLEMENTINE:
No, get the fuck away!

1375
01:39:21.001 --> 01:39:24.749
Hey, Clementine.
Nice to see you.

1376
01:39:31.876 --> 01:39:35.708
JOEL ON TAPE: I mean,
she's smart, I think,
but not educated.

1377
01:39:36.209 --> 01:39:38.708
I couldn't talk to her
about books.

1378
01:39:38.876 --> 01:39:41.499
She's more of
a magazine-reading girl.

1379
01:39:42.168 --> 01:39:45.208
Her vocabulary leaves
something to be desired.

1380
01:39:45.709 --> 01:39:48.208
The truth is,
I was embarrassed in public,

1381
01:39:48.293 --> 01:39:51.916
Hi.
Because she would pronounce
"library," "li-berry."

1382
01:39:57.209 --> 01:39:58.541
Look what I found.

1383
01:39:58.625 --> 01:40:02.541
JOEL: I think if there's
a truly seductive quality
about Clementine,

1384
01:40:02.625 --> 01:40:06.374
it's that her personality
promises to take you
out of the mundane.

1385
01:40:08.168 --> 01:40:10.332
Made me look skinny.

1386
01:40:10.417 --> 01:40:14.167
An amazing, burning meteorite
will carry you
to another world

1387
01:40:14.251 --> 01:40:16.167
where things are exciting.

1388
01:40:18.542 --> 01:40:22.749
But what you quickly learn
is that it's really
an elaborate ruse.

1389
01:40:23.375 --> 01:40:25.416
I'm sorry I yelled at you.

1390
01:40:26.709 --> 01:40:28.041
It's okay.

1391
01:40:33.001 --> 01:40:36.250
I really like you.
I hate that I said
mean things about you.

1392
01:40:36.333 --> 01:40:38.374
Let me turn this off, okay?

1393
01:40:39.209 --> 01:40:40.958
That's only fair.

1394
01:40:44.375 --> 01:40:47.624
JOEL: The whole thing
with the hair,
it's all bullshit.

1395
01:40:47.709 --> 01:40:49.958
I really like your hair.

1396
01:40:50.042 --> 01:40:51.249
Thank you.

1397
01:40:51.709 --> 01:40:52.916
I do.

1398
01:40:56.292 --> 01:40:58.125
You want a drink or something?

1399
01:40:58.209 --> 01:40:59.875
Do you have any whiskey?

1400
01:41:01.459 --> 01:41:06.208
JOEL: I didn't think
her sex was motivated.

1401
01:41:06.542 --> 01:41:10.458
I saw it clearly
the last night we were
together. It wasn't sexy.

1402
01:41:10.542 --> 01:41:12.958
It was just sad.

1403
01:41:14.168 --> 01:41:16.291
Sorry,
I thought there was more.

1404
01:41:16.417 --> 01:41:19.708
JOEL: The only way Clem thinks
she can get people to like her

1405
01:41:19.792 --> 01:41:21.499
is to fuck them.

1406
01:41:22.667 --> 01:41:26.583
Or at least dangle
the possibility of getting
fucked in front of them.

1407
01:41:26.667 --> 01:41:30.125
I think she's
so desperate and insecure

1408
01:41:31.168 --> 01:41:34.374
that she'll sooner or later
go around fucking everybody.

1409
01:41:34.459 --> 01:41:35.583
I don't do that.

1410
01:41:35.667 --> 01:41:38.083
JOEL: I wouldn't
think that about you.

1411
01:41:38.292 --> 01:41:40.332
Because I don't.
I know.

1412
01:41:40.542 --> 01:41:43.416
It hurts me
that you said that,
because I don't do that.

1413
01:41:43.500 --> 01:41:45.207
I'm so sorry.
I'm sorry about all this.

1414
01:41:45.292 --> 01:41:49.041
I'm going to go.
I'm a little confused.

1415
01:41:49.126 --> 01:41:51.875
I don't really think
I can be here.

1416
01:41:58.834 --> 01:41:59.833
Bye.

1417
01:42:00.542 --> 01:42:02.624
JOEL: I really thought
I knew her so well.

1418
01:42:02.709 --> 01:42:04.708
It was nice meeting you
and all.

1419
01:42:07.542 --> 01:42:10.875
JOEL: What a loss to spend
that much time with someone,

1420
01:42:10.959 --> 01:42:13.583
only to find out
that she's a stranger.

1421
01:42:18.500 --> 01:42:19.583
Wait.

1422
01:42:22.542 --> 01:42:24.708
What?
I don't know. Just wait.

1423
01:42:24.834 --> 01:42:29.583
What do you want, Joel?
I want you to wait
for a while.

1424
01:42:44.167 --> 01:42:46.166
Okay.
Really?

1425
01:42:46.959 --> 01:42:50.875
I'm not a concept,
just a fucked-up girl
looking for my peace of mind.

1426
01:42:50.959 --> 01:42:52.458
I'm not perfect.

1427
01:42:52.542 --> 01:42:55.000
I can't see anything
that I don't like about you.

1428
01:42:55.084 --> 01:42:57.458
But you will.
Right now I can't.

1429
01:42:57.917 --> 01:42:59.583
You will think of things.

1430
01:42:59.667 --> 01:43:01.541
And I'll get bored with you
and feel trapped,

1431
01:43:01.625 --> 01:43:04.041
because that's what happens
with me.

1432
01:43:05.500 --> 01:43:06.583
Okay.

1433
01:43:11.084 --> 01:43:12.207
Okay.

1434
01:43:16.876 --> 01:43:18.041
Okay.
